Date: Tue, 04 Sep 2018 10:48:12 +0000
Subject: What's the best way to calculate predictions (including random effects and spatial spde) based a new data set and inla model?
Message-ID: <jygilSMpm4U.geVKfJvGBQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/jygilSMpm4U/m/geVKfJvGBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all,

I have runned a model including random effect and spatial spde. Now I would like to calculate the predictions on a new dataset, including the random effect and spatial effects. I havent figured out an efficient way to do it. What's the best way to do it, without wasting time in estimating the model again?

Thanks

Regards,
Chun

From u9940b4fcc153c7d7 at groups.google.com  Tue Sep  4 10:50:26 2018
From: u9940b4fcc153c7d7 at groups.google.com (Haakon Bakka)
Date: Tue, 04 Sep 2018 10:50:26 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] Why adding a spatial spde gives extremely bad dic performance
Message-ID: <DvRdHh7CzNs.4WA2vbNoBQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <DvRdHh7CzNs.mdq9Pfu-BQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <DvRdHh7CzNs.mdq9Pfu-BQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/DvRdHh7CzNs/m/4WA2vbNoBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Chun,

Even though the posterior mean is small does not mean the random field is not used / uninformative. I am not surprised that the DIC can sometimes be worse.

I recommend trying the pc priors, and making the shrinkage stronger than what we usually use. See e.g.
https://haakonbakka.bitbucket.io/btopic108.html#5_the_model
Make the prior median for sigma small and the prior median for range big, this may improve the DIC of the spatial model.

Best,
Haakon

